# Vivat Bus interface rules

- Use shadcn/ui primitives for controls, forms, tables, dialogs, sheets, menus, tabs, alerts, badges, progress and skeleton states. Do not hand-build equivalents from raw elements.
- Fetch React Bits components from its current registry. Use motion only when it explains state or hierarchy and always honor reduced motion.
- Put the page title and description in `AppShell`. Never repeat either in page content.
- Put page-local search immediately after the page identity in the top bar. Keep cross-entity search in the `Command` palette (`Ctrl/Cmd+K`).
- Use the shared entity view for database-backed collections. Table is the default; enable gallery, kanban or calendar only when the data supports that view.
- Tables expose useful columns by default and let the user reveal the remaining API/database fields. Keep numeric and time columns tabular.
- Collection rows support left-side checkbox selection, bulk actions and a right-click context menu with the same core actions available through visible controls.
- Company and interface settings are opened from the profile menu. Do not add settings to primary sidebar navigation.
- Keep the sidebar and top bar aligned to the same top edge and height. Logos use `BrandMark` and must remain legible in collapsed, desktop and mobile states.
- Status uses semantic color badges. Gold is reserved for primary actions, meaningful progress and brand signals.
- Verify responsive behavior at phone and desktop widths, keyboard access, loading/error/empty states, typecheck, lint and production build before pushing.
